NOTE: the per-Profile/per-Lint example code-block was lost during initial bead creation (shell parsed the backticks as command substitution). The intended example:

    /// CA/Browser Forum TLS Baseline Requirements profile.
    ///
    /// Canonical source: [TLS BR §7.1.2.7.12 (Subscriber Certificate Subject Alternative Name)](https://github.com/cabforum/servercert/blob/main/docs/BR.md#712712-subscriber-certificate-subject-alternative-name)
    ///
    /// ... (existing rustdoc continues here) ...

Anchor convention: GitHub auto-generates section anchors from heading text by lowercasing, dropping spaces, and stripping punctuation. So heading "##### 7.1.2.7.12 Subscriber Certificate Subject Alternative Name" becomes anchor "#712712-subscriber-certificate-subject-alternative-name". Verify each anchor resolves before committing -- GitHub's exact slugification can include edge cases (consecutive spaces, em-dashes, etc.). Quick verify: curl -fsSL the URL; nonzero exit means the anchor is wrong.
